  "scope": "The first real shell produced typed Exit 0 followed by a browser-reported clean Close 1000. The ended pane was observed while an old running poll was held. Natural absence of the exact original allocation and release of its manual lease were confirmed in 24 polls over 16.009196 seconds, before one UI Restart. Restart returned HTTP 409. The original C069 helper asserted status before reading the body; no Restart problem body or body hash was retained. The screenshot is separate UI evidence, not a recovered response body or numeric admission operands. The original result retains one pending mutation; exact-container-leftovers and final-source-and-inventory remain failed-or-unsettled. No successful Restart, replacement allocation, second Exit 7, or completed warm recovery was observed. Later independent closure found three known identities absent, two browser zombies, and empty container, volume, and ledger inventories. That later sample does not certify remote mutation settlement or retroactively pass automatic cleanup.",
